.TH "PB-SESSION-DELETE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-session-delete - Delete a closed terminal session record


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb session delete [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a closed terminal session record

.PP
Delete a closed non-default terminal session record, or use --all for all such records in the environment. Close a running terminal first. With --all, run the command once to receive a short-lived confirmation token, then run the displayed command to proceed. the confirmation code confirms only single-session deletion.

.PP
Terminal sessions persist independently of a single connection and can be reattached after a disconnect. Sharing grants explicit access to a named session. Closing, deleting, and removing a participant have different effects; inspect the selected session before acting.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	delete all sessions in the environment

.PP
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	six-character confirmation code from the preview

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for delete

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-session(1)\fP
